    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Google describes Gemini as its AI assistant for writing, planning, brainstorming, and more, and presents it as generative AI. The company is a public company founded in 1998, headquartered in Mountain View, CA, USA, and traded as GOOGL. It reported revenue of $402,836,000,000 for the fiscal year ended 2025-12-31 in a 10-K filing.\n\nThe records track several Google AI products. Gemini is a general LLM assistant. Google AI Studio is for model prototyping. Google Med-PaLM / MedLM is a medical LLM with notes on clinical reasoning, healthcare data, HIPAA BAA requirement, and diagnostic liability. Google Drive AI and Google Meet AI cover Workspace data and meeting summaries. NotebookLM provides document grounding. TensorFlow / Keras is an ML framework with notes on model serialization risks and custom model governance.\n\nGoogle is registered with the SEC under CIK 0001652044. The data lists 281 legal exposure entries in California. It also lists MCP servers for Google Ads, Google News, Google Search Console, Google OAuth, Google Forms, Google Calendar, and Google Trends.",
